[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5079425291","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121706#issuecomment-5079425291","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121706","id":5079425291,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLsHhCw","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-25T17:11:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-25T17:11:34Z","body":"Nearest in this case means the shape that is most overlapping with the cone. This function is not suitable for finding the closest hit to the origin of the cone. You could e.g. use `intersect_shape` and sort the resulting colliding shapes on distance from the origin.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5079425291/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5079477495","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121706#issuecomment-5079477495","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121706","id":5079477495,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLsKs9w","user":{"login":"Megmachunian","id":10481838,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDgxODM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10481838?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian","html_url":"https://github.com/Megmachunian","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Megmachunian/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-25T17:26:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-25T17:27:17Z","body":"Thanks for clarifying what nearest means in this case, that makes sense.\n\nI'm not sure that using intersect shape would consistently work in this case. `intersect_shape` doesn't return a collision point, and using the position of the object will result in larger objects (i.e. walls and floors) being incorrectly sorted. My next attempt will be to use `collide_shape` and then use `intersect_ray` to the shortest collision point","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5079477495/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]